        };
      case 'electrical_hazard':
        return {
          safety: "!!  ELECTRICAL HAZARD: Do NOT touch anything wet or any electrical devices. Stay back from the area. If you can safely reach your electrical panel, turn off the breaker for that area. Do NOT step in any water.",
          followUp: "Are you away from the affected area?",
          problemType: 'leak'
        };
      case 'sewage_emergency':
        return {
          safety: "!!  SEWAGE BACKUP: Stop using ALL water and drains right now - toilets, sinks, everything. This prevents more backup. Keep people and pets away from the affected area. This is a health hazard.",
          followUp: "Is it still actively backing up?",
          problemType: 'sewer_backup'
        };
      case 'heater_flooding':
        return {
          safety: "!!  WATER HEATER FLOODING: Turn off the water supply to the heater if you can reach it safely. The cold water inlet valve is usually on top. Stay away from any electrical outlets near the water. If it's gas, turn off the gas valve too.",
          followUp: "Were you able to turn off the water to the heater?",
          problemType: 'water_heater_leaking'
        };
      case 'pipe_burst':
        return {
          safety: "!!  BURST PIPE: Find your main water shutoff and turn it off NOW if you can. It's usually near the water meter or where the main line enters your house. This will stop the flooding.",
          followUp: "Were you able to turn off the water?",
          problemType: 'pipe_burst'
        };
      case 'pump_failure':
        return {
          safety: "!!  PUMP ALARM: Stop using water and drains immediately. If you have a basement, check if water is rising and stay clear of any standing water near electrical outlets.",
          followUp: "Is water backing up or rising right now?",
          problemType: 'ejector_pump_alarm'
        };
      case 'flooding':
        return {
          safety: "!!  FLOODING: Stay out of standing water, especially near electrical outlets or appliances. If safe, turn off the main water supply. Don't use any electrical devices in wet areas.",
          followUp: "Is water still coming in?",
          problemType: 'sewer_basement_flood'
        };
      case 'cant_shutoff':
        return {
          safety: "!!  CAN'T SHUT OFF WATER: Your main shutoff valve is usually near the water meter (often in the basement, crawlspace, or outside near the street). It's a wheel or lever valve. Turn it clockwise to close. If you can't find it or it won't turn, call your water company's emergency line - they can shut it off at the street.",
          followUp: "Were you able to find the shutoff?",
          problemType: 'pipe_burst'
        };
      case 'active_leak':
        return {
          safety: "!!  ACTIVE LEAK: If you can safely reach the shutoff valve for that area, turn it off. Put buckets or towels under the leak. Stay away from electrical outlets near the water.",
          followUp: "Is water still coming through?",
          problemType: 'leak'
        };
      case 'active_water':
        return {
          safety: "!!  WATER WON'T STOP: Find your main water shutoff valve and turn it off. It's usually near the water meter or where the main line enters your house. This will stop all water flow.",
          followUp: "Were you able to find and turn off the main valve?",
          problemType: 'pipe_burst'
        };
      case 'heater_critical':
        return {
          safety: "!!  WATER HEATER DANGER: Stay back from the unit - hot water or steam can cause severe burns. Don't touch it. If it's making rumbling, hissing, or banging noises, keep everyone away. If it's gas, turn off the gas valve to the heater if you can do it safely from a distance.",
          followUp: "Is it still making noise or leaking?",
          problemType: 'water_heater_leaking'
        };
      default:
        return {
          safety: "!!  URGENT: If water is flowing, try to turn off the main water valve. Stay away from standing water near electrical outlets. Keep people and pets clear of the affected area.",
          followUp: "Is the situation still getting worse?",
          problemType: 'leak'
        };
    }
  }
};

